From 03d504f4977197aa484702798876f3defd6188df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 06:05:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Supervisor on the local verifier: every chain read, receipt,
 nonce and submission through the selected authority

supervisor.js: with the operator's explicit verifier selection, its one chainClient and its operator wallet use the
chain-authority transport (CHAIN_AUTHORITY) instead of the provider pool, so the claim decision, ledger mirror, catalog
moderation, sessions, prices, registry, bond, proofs/settlement/payouts, receipts, the release resolver and the boot nonce
fence are all answered by the verifier, and every transaction is submitted only through the own backend; BASE_RPC(S) and
the public defaults are never contacted. Before anything is signed - sendOperatorTx, sendLeaseTx, signAndSendRelease,
fenceNonce - actionGate requires a fresh verified head (and, to submit, a backend bound to the verifier's chain): a failing
gate signs nothing and consumes no nonce. App-funded leases and the owner nomination read through the same ONE authority.
/v1/health reports the authority and its last gate. An invalid selection refuses every chain operation; unset is the
provider pool exactly as before (legacy, never claimed as independent).
addressbook.js: under the verifier the admin AddressBook is read from block-pinned verified snapshots, so the
administrator's migrations still reach the host with no provider (book polling kept; pins mode unchanged).
docs/network/supervisor-chain-authority.md: the routing, the trust of each answer and the path-by-path inventory, with the
one remaining gate (G1: payment-event completeness: inclusion is proven, omission is not detectable).
